    "text": "",
    "media": "1238.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1241,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:12:43+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Unopened items found along the side of the road. After a holiday party of visiting strangers, whenever you are many things are often left behind, either intentionally, or maybe unintentionally.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1242,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:12:44+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1242.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1243,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:12:44+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1243.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1244,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:16:00+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Here is a different sort of item that I am finding to be commonly left behind by kids.  These torches have a useful electric spark lighter for my gas stove, and they are refillable. So often I only need one so choose the best as I find and  upgrade along the way.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1245,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:16:08+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1245.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1246,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:17:07+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Irresponsible use of a firearm, most likely young white males.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1247,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:17:16+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1247.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1248,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:19:26+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Another campsite, another tree. This is a salt-cedar tree, I believe. Short, but offers nice shade and ground cover.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1249,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:19:44+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1249.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1250,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:19:44+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1250.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1251,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:25:53+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "32.76572° N, 115.27004° W\n\nHere's the geo-coordinates of a wonderful hot spring along the Interstate highway where thousands pass by through the barren desert each day and don't even know it's there.  \n\nMost of the time I have the place to myself. \n\nMy salt-cedar campsite above is located less than a mile away.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1252,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:26:00+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "",
    "media": "1252.jpg"
  },
  {
    "id": 1253,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:27:35+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "The hot spring is not obvious to highway traffic. It's public and free, there's parking and a bathroom.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1254,
    "date": "2021-11-17T20:27:50+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
